        "subject": "LU-19309 lnet: do not mark a gateway peer deleted",
        "message": "LU-19309 lnet: do not mark a gateway peer deleted\n\nA mount, or \"lnetctl peer add\", can name a NID of a gateway peer.\nThen the lnet_discovery thread can spin without end, and the\nwatchdog reports a soft lockup.\n\nlnet_peer_add() calls lnet_peer_del() for that peer.\nlnet_peer_del_locked() sets LNET_PEER_MARK_DELETED, but it keeps\neach peer NI of a gateway. A message to the peer then calls\nlnet_initiate_peer_discovery(). lnet_discover_peer_locked() stops on\nMARK_DELETED, and the message goes back on lp_dc_pendq. The discovery\nthread resends it at once, and the loop starts again.\n\nlnet_peer_del() now returns -EBUSY for a gateway before it cancels\ndiscovery or sets MARK_DELETED. One CERROR replaces the message for\neach peer NI. The caller holds ln_api_mutex, so a route cannot change\nafter the check. Test 114 adds this case.\n\n    3 VMs, peer add --lock_prim of the gateway, push, lst\n    without the fix: 5 of 5 spin, soft lockup panic\n    with the fix:    0 of 15 spin, lst RPC completes\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: fd32cd817cba (\"LU-13895 lnet: Prevent discovery on deleted peer\")\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: Ic4b8420dc543871d478c068d9be9a6314c3f99f3\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
